{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "The board's identity is ADAPTER-DECLARED and now verifiable. RCA 2026-07-02: an ad-hoc `projectsV2` discovery query resolved the wrong project by display-name resemblance, and every read afterwards inherited that resolution and reported on it confidently. Three things change. The generated adapter renders the pin (`- Board pin: <owner>/projects/<n>`) when the enabled provider carries one, and renders NOTHING when it does not -- a lane with no pin gets no line rather than a line that guesses. `backlog-provider-board-check` compares the identity recorded in every synced goal source against that pin and BLOCKS on a mismatch, on the same exit-1 path as drift, because a board that is not the pinned board is not out of date -- it is the wrong board; its ok path now prints `board_identity:` so a passing gate is distinguishable from a gate that did not run. A source recording no identity is never guessed about.",
    "A board read that saw part of the board now SAYS so. `goal_tracker_board_position_map` was a single un-cursored `items(first:100)` page, so on any board past a hundred items every later item was missing from the authoritative order and the selection site ranked it by a synthetic `len(position_map) + position` -- real board order and fallback order in one sort key. It now paginates to the same ceiling the verified read uses, and returns an EMPTY map rather than a partial one on any mid-pagination failure, because a half-filled map looks authoritative while silently ranking the items it contains above every item it does not. The two warning-only callers (`provider_board_business_lead_gaps`, `lane_unplaced_customer_facing_issues`) still return [] on an unreadable board but now print a `board read incomplete` warning first: both report what is MISSING, so an unreadable board produced the most reassuring possible answer from the least evidence.",
    "Policy states both rules: a queried project number differing from the configured `projectNumber` is blocking drift and not a fallback candidate, and operator-observed UI state beats an agent's API result rather than losing to it -- arguing with operator evidence is a stop-the-line defect. The new `github-projects-reads` skill carries the four read-side controls with the surface traps that produced them."
  ],
